    "K1.4-candidate, round 3: the identity-rendering redesign after review 02 of H 14a7ef48 (K14C-R02-01), under brief 03 (read by commit at 2a95a49a), design 03 with its addendum 01, design check 03 (read by commit at 62092a70) and owner choice 04. Rounds 1 and 2 stand as their records give them: owner release 01; brief 01; design 01 with addendum 01; design 02; owner choices 01 to 03; implementation reports 01 and 02. The candidate: tests/conformance/k0-candidate/{kernel-candidate,canonical-json,fake-driver}.ts, driving ExecutionCoordinator through the @arrokothi/kernel package root. Its tests: verdicts (KC-3: 12 PASS and 3 REFUSED, pinned exactly), blindness (KC-2), boundary (KC-1 import guard, KC-5 locator), ablations (KC-1), conventions, identity and identity-search. Its README is the locator and pin contract for the benchmark's E1.",
    "No Kernel source change: packages is preserved whole at B, with package.json, package-lock.json and tsconfig.json. The fixture's scenarios, runner, oracle and coverage are preserved at B; decision 4 changes comments in tests/conformance/k0/{candidate,fixture,protocol-vocabulary}.ts, the refusal control's reason string, and refusal.test.ts's header and describe title. scripts and tests/tooling are preserved at B: registering the ablations changed no packet tool.",
    "One architecture guard is extended by name: kernel-landing-zone.test.ts lists the three candidate files that import the Kernel package root. The ablation test loads each edited temporary copy of the Kernel source in a child process, from a generated entry file with literal imports, so the literal-import guard is preserved at B.",
    "Round 3, K14C-R02-01 (design 03): every translated identity position of an Observation is the value of one name ledger per scope (Executions over the run; wait generations and Events per native Execution; input and timeout Events share the Event ledger). The map is injective and never changes during a run; a name attaches only at the Kernel answer that names its ID; a reference resolves through the same ledger. A Kernel answer is checked against the inspection made after it and a contradiction throws (addendum 01 section A1). The claim is about IDs within one run: a wrong ID that is consistent from its first appearance is not detected (017 L-39). ingressRefused and emissions are outside the rule (017 L-42). Round 2's timeout name table is replaced.",
    "Round 3, verification: identity-search.test.ts runs 4,126 skeleton runs (every assignment with at most two non-ordinary name slots; 344 of them with a changed-ID fault at a duplicate fire), judged by an independent oracle in identity-lab.ts that never reads the candidate's ledger. Three-way name interactions are covered only by the named witnesses. The seven mechanism mutants M1 to M7 are cases k14-candidate.identity-m1 to -m7 of mutations.json, run through identity-probe.mjs with a coverage family and seven unread hold-register entries; they are mechanism_witness records with no conformance or correction credit (017 L-44). scripts and tests/tooling are preserved at B.",
